#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179458 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44b96053-1ffa-56d3-8129-15ada765b9a7" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Positive Decimals From Decimals With Halves"}] :question/id #uuid "0e9e4dd1-3161-5d3c-afab-5514e1c2d0d4" :question/math-academy-id "e-13383" :question/problem "What is $-2.5 - 4.5$?" :question/worked-solution "To subtract $4.5$ from $-2.5$, we break up $4.5$ into its whole number part ($4$) and its decimal part ($0.5$) and proceed in two steps.\n\n- First, we subtract the whole number part. We start at $-2.5$ on the number line and move $4$ places to the left, which brings us to $-6.5$.\n- Then, we subtract the decimal part. We move the remaining $0.5$ places to the left, leaving us at $-7$.\n\n![](images/53/53e5b15019c3189519b0fb4801e2ead2d9cd954d7da84640bb684215e53aca7a.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n-2.5 - 4.5 = -7.0\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179459 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "507d4d46-699c-5b4f-a010-66aec6abef67" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Positive Decimals From Decimals"}] :question/id #uuid "6bd42661-9814-51ce-a359-39bd54aff3e7" :question/math-academy-id "e-13384" :question/problem "What is the value of $4.6-7.7$?" :question/worked-solution "Since $7.7$ is larger than $4.6$, the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem, which is to carry out the subtraction in the reverse order:\n\n$$\n7.7 - 4.6 = 3.1\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n4.6-7.7 = -3.1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179460 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "778ae1c8-c651-56f1-ab58-1817d3fe4bb9" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Positive Decimals From Decimals With Unequal Numbers of Decimals"}] :question/id #uuid "45b45968-91b2-5ed4-86c2-51d31e02b714" :question/math-academy-id "e-13385" :question/problem "What is the value of $-1.25-3.3$?" :question/worked-solution "Since $3.3$ is larger than $1.25$, the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem, which is to add their absolute values:\n\n$$\n1.25+3.3 = 4.55\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-1.25-3.3 = -4.55\n$$"}]}
